-- =============================================================================
-- The result of running a semantics: a value, a gap, or a timeout.
--
-- Shared by both runners -- the Java fragment's evaluator (`Formal/JavaEval.ard`)
-- and λ□'s (`Formal/LambdaBoxRun.ard`) -- which is the whole reason it is a
-- module of its own rather than living in either.
--
-- `rStuck` ("the semantics does not define this") is deliberately distinct from
-- `rOutOfFuel` ("the clock ran out"). A differential test needs the difference:
-- the first is a real disagreement, the second only a budget that was too small.
-- Collapsing both into `Maybe` would report the second as the first.
--
-- The clock discipline itself is Owens-Myreen-Kumar-Tan, "Functional Big-Step
-- Semantics" (ESOP 2016); `bindRes` is the functional answer to Charguéraud's
-- observation that exceptions otherwise duplicate every rule ("Pretty-Big-Step
-- Semantics", ESOP 2013), paid for once instead of per rule.
-- =============================================================================

\data Res (A : \Type)
  | rOk A
  | rStuck
  | rOutOfFuel

\func bindRes {A B : \Type} (r : Res A) (f : A -> Res B) : Res B \elim r
  | rOk a => f a
  | rStuck => rStuck
  | rOutOfFuel => rOutOfFuel
